# Artifacts must survive a round trip byte-for-byte.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is normal on Windows, and without this git would store
# model_config.json and xgb_population.json with LF and check them out with
# CRLF. The bytes on disk would then differ from the bytes committed, and the
# SHA-256 fingerprints in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 would fail on a fresh clone
# — for a reason that looks nothing like line endings.
#
# The .keras/.npz/.pkl files are detected as binary anyway; the JSON ones are
# the trap. Marking the whole tree is simpler than remembering which is which.
artifacts/** -text
